# pip 26.x vendors msgpack 1.1.2 internally for its own inter-process
# communication. This is pip's private dependency — it is never exposed to
# user-controlled input in our application. Fix requires a pip release that
# upgrades its vendored copy; not actionable on our end.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# The python:3.x-slim base image embeds an OCI SBOM that lists setuptools
# 70.3.0. Our Dockerfiles explicitly upgrade setuptools to >=78.1.1 (installed
# version: 84.0.0), but Trivy surfaces the stale SBOM entry alongside the
# real installation. The installed version is clean.
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890

# pip 25.x vendors urllib3 2.7.0 internally (pip/_vendor/urllib3). Our
# application installs urllib3>=2.8.0 as a direct dependency, so the runtime
# copy is patched. The pip-vendored copy is only used during image build (pip
# install) and is not reachable by our application code.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97688
CVE-2026-97689
